              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Want a touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F80</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,499.99</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Want a wide deck</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F85</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,999.99</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            For full reviews, see the <a href="/sole-f63-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Sole F63</a>, <a href="/sole-f65-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">F65</a>, <a href="/sole-f80-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">F80</a> and <a href="/sole-f85-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">F85</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="when" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>When Sole Treadmills Are Cheapest</h2>
<p>
            On 22 November 2026 every in-stock Sole was already $100 to $300 below its regular price, ahead of Black Friday.
            Sole&rsquo;s regular prices are rarely what buyers pay: holiday sales, New Year promotions and clearance of
            outgoing models are the usual times to buy. Our <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best time of year to buy a treadmill</a> and <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill Black Friday deals</a> track the patterns.
          </p>
        </div>


        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Where People Go Wrong When Pricing a Sole Treadmill</h2>
          <p>Most of these come from comparing sticker prices and ignoring what comes with them.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Paying the regular price</h3>
              <p>Every in-stock Sole was $100 to $300 off on 22 November 2026. Sole’s regular price is a reference, not the usual selling price.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Buying a touchscreen you will not use</h3>
              <p>The F80 costs $300 more than the F65 for a screen, with the same deck. If you stream from a tablet anyway, the F63 or F65 is the better value.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Forgetting delivery</h3>
              <p>Standard delivery is curbside freight. A heavy treadmill left at the kerb needs two people and a plan, or the paid in-room upgrade.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Not asking about parts and labour</h3>
              <p>Sole’s pages state lifetime frame and motor but not parts and labour. Get those terms in writing before you compare Sole against Horizon or Spirit.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">A Sole treadmill costs $899.99 to $2,899.99 on Sole&rsquo;s store, and most buyers spend
            $1,099.99 (F63) to $1,999.99 (F85)</strong>, with no monthly subscription on top.
          </p>
          <p>
            For running without a screen, the F63 or F65 is the value pick; pay for the F80 or F85 only if you want the
            touchscreen or the wider deck. Buy in a sale, plan for curbside delivery, and ask Sole for the parts and
            labour terms. Our <a href="/sole-fitness/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Sole guide</a> covers the range.
          </p>
        </div>

