        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does a Sole treadmill need a subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Sole's product pages list no monthly subscription and a free SOLE+ app. You can stream other apps on your own tablet or, on the touchscreen models, on the built-in screen where Sole allows it, but nothing is required to use the treadmill.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the cheapest Sole treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The F50, at $899.99 on Sole's store on 22 November 2026, down from $999.99. It tops out at 10 mph on a 20 by 55-inch deck, so it suits walking and jogging; the F63 at $1,099.99 is the cheapest Sole built for running.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Sole F65 worth $100 more than the F63?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 22 November 2026 it was only $100 more on Sole's store and adds a 3.25 HP motor instead of 3.0 HP and a 350 lb rating instead of 325 lb, on the same 20 by 60-inch deck. If you are near the F63's limit or run often, it is a small price for the extra headroom.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Sole treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              From $899.99 for the F50 to $2,899.99 for the TT8 on Sole's US store on 22 November 2026. The F63 was $1,099.99, the F65 $1,199.99, the F80 $1,499.99, the F83 $1,699.99, the F85 $1,999.99 and the F89 $2,699.99.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Sole F80?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $1,499.99 on Sole's store on 22 November 2026, down from $1,599.99. It has a 10.1-inch touchscreen, 12 mph and a 20 by 60-inch deck.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Sole charge a monthly subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Sole's product pages list no monthly subscription and a free SOLE+ app, which makes a Sole cheaper over five years than treadmills that need a paid class membership.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the cheapest Sole treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The F50, at $899.99 on Sole's store on 22 November 2026 (regular $999.99). It tops out at 10 mph on a 55-inch deck, so the $1,099.99 F63 is the cheapest Sole built for running.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a Sole treadmill worth the money?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For runners who want a solid deck and no subscription, yes: the F63 gives a 60-inch deck, 12 mph and a lifetime frame and motor warranty for $1,099.99. Ask Sole for the parts and labour terms, which its product pages did not state.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is Sole cheaper on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not on 21 and 22 November 2026: the F63 and F65 were the same price on Amazon as on Sole's store. Compare the seller, delivery terms and return policy before choosing.
            </p>
